course: dictionary
lesson: 4163
title: Words for players who guard the goal
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A goalie is the player who stands in the goal and tries to stop the ball or puck from going in. Goalie is a short, friendly word for goalkeeper, so the two words mean the same thing. The word goal is a clue: a goalie guards the goal.
explain: Read this: «A cricket or hockey ball is hard enough to break bones, so close fielders and goalies wear helmets and pads.» The words hard enough to break bones show that goalies face hard balls, so they need protection. Ask yourself: who guards the goal? That is the goalie.
explain: Goalie is used in many games: football (soccer), hockey, ice hockey, handball, netball and water polo. In playground games children take turns being the goalie. Check your meaning by swapping it in: «The goalie saved it» still makes sense if goalie means the player who stops the ball from going in.
fact: A goalie is the player who stands in the goal and tries to stop the ball or puck from going in.
fact: Goalie is a short, friendly word for goalkeeper.
fact: Goalies play in football (soccer), hockey, ice hockey, handball, netball and water polo.
fact: «Play in goal» means to be the goalie, and «goalie gloves» are gloves a goalie wears.
fact: «Best goalie ever!» is a phrase of praise for a goalie who plays very well.
exercise: In «Best goalie ever!», what does goalie mean? | *The player who stands in the goal and tries to stop the ball | A cake shaped like a goal | The referee who blows the whistle | The player who scores the most goals
exercise: Goalie is a short, friendly word for which longer word? | goalpost | fielder | *goalkeeper | referee
exercise: «A cricket or hockey ball is hard enough to break bones, so close fielders and goalies wear helmets and pads.» Why do goalies wear helmets and pads? | Because the game is water polo | To look smart on the pitch | *To protect them from a hard ball | Because they are always cold
test: Which word is a short, friendly word for goalkeeper? | referee | striker | *goalie
test: Which game is played with a puck? | *ice hockey | netball | handball
exam: In «A tired brain reacts more slowly and makes worse choices, which keepers, goalies and batters notice first.», what do keepers, goalies and batters have in common? | They are very slow runners | They are types of brain | They are animals that live in the sea | *They are players in sport who need quick reactions
